WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:07.969
Hey Team it’s Charlie and this week for
my bonus video I wanted to do an update on

00:00:07.969 --> 00:00:12.380
this year’s Christmas Special and my favorite
guest characters from all the specials.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:18.980
They just announced most if not all of this
years big guest stars and it’s a pretty

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:19.980
exciting group.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.390
The giveaway is still running till I post
my Q&amp;A tomorrow, I’ll explain again at the

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.699
end of the video in case you have absolutely
no idea what I’m talking about.

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:29.460
Starting off with Christmas Special Updates:

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:37.890
They just officially announced these people
will guest star Nick Frost of Cornetto Fame,

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:43.920
Patrick Troughton the second doctor’s son,
Nathan McMullen from Misfits, Natalie Gumede

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:49.719
from Coronation Street and Faye Marsay from
Glue.

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:54.039
Nick Frost was seen earlier this week walking
around the set with Dan Starkey who plays

00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:55.039
Strax.

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:59.229
They’ve been filming the special at St Mellons
Golf Club and Vaendre Hall in Cardiff.

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:08.250
Here’s a couple pictures of the manor they’ve
been filming around.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.030
Now that they’ve confirmed Frost it also
sounds like the Paternoster Gang or at least

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:17.380
Strax will be in the special.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.220
Which explains why they’re filming near
a victorian looking manor.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:25.979
They might be back in Victorian times.

00:01:25.979 --> 00:01:29.953
No word on who Nick Frost is playing but the
best rumor I’ve seen is that it’s Santa

00:01:29.953 --> 00:01:32.590
Claus or someone in a very santa like suit.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.850
It is Christmas after all so there might be
some truth to that.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:41.899
I feel like now that two thirds of the Cornetto
gang have been on Doctor Who, Edgar Wright

00:01:41.899 --> 00:01:44.579
will have to cave and direct an episode soon.

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:47.759
Wouldn’t it be crazy if they got all three
of them together for the same episode.

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:51.440
It would totally kill Doctor Who’s budget,
but it’s fun to imagine.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.390
Edgar Wright actually said that Russell T.
Davies offered him the job of directing the

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:00.359
2005 debut of series 1 Rose.

00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:03.429
But he had to turn it down because he was
working on Shawn of The Dead.

00:02:03.429 --> 00:02:10.310
He said his mother still hasn’t forgiven
him.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.360
No idea yet who Patrick Troughton or any of
the other guest cast are playing or what the

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.360
story is going to be.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.290
There’s really two ways it could go, it
could be a straight one-off like the 2011

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.930
christmas special, the Doctor, the Widow and
the Wardrobe.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.260
Or it could deal with the aftermath of the
series 8 finale.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.920
Right now with all the rumors going around
about Jenna Coleman leaving, I’m thinking

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:33.090
it will be the second option.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.790
And be a bookend to the Missy storyline, the
doctor’s face and explaining how they’ll

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.700
proceed into series 9 next year.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:45.739
With all the teasers about Clara having problems
trying to live a normal life and be a companion

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:50.810
I’m starting to think she will be moving
on.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.870
But here’s a big question, look at some
of what’s happening in the teaser for episode

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.950
6 and tell me.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.269
Does this look like the face of a companion
that’s going to stay or does it look like

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:04.900
Clara wants to have a go at being normal.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:09.819
I’m still crying about the way Amy and Rory
left, so if Clara really does leave I can

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:22.870
only imagine how it will go down.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:28.650
With the Christmas Special In Mind, here’s
my Top 5 Guest Actors to star a Special, just

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.040
Christmas Specials.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.860
Number 5 - Lindsay Duncan in Waters of Mars

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:37.900
Of all the female guest stars during the David
Tennant Specials she felt like the most badass.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:46.340
And how cool was it that she showed up in
Sherlock Series 3 last year?

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:58.510
I’m mostly just talking about the actors
themselves here, but I liked her character

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:02.130
adelaide brooks the most out of the temporary
companions.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:11.080
Definitely the smartest and she was one of
the few female companions that didn’t automatically

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.469
start fawning over the doctor.

00:04:13.469 --> 00:04:18.150
To be fair, they were being hunted down systematically,
so no much time for romance on Mars.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.330
Number 4 - Richard E Grant in The Snowmen

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:24.950
He’s one of the few actors I could legitimately
be afraid of without having to put on a lot

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:29.260
of prosthetics or voice manipulation like
with Nicholas Briggs doing Dalek voice.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:35.670
There are a lot of things you could say about
the series since Moffat took over as showrunner,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.450
but I feel like he really pushed for the celebrity
guest stars in the specials.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.880
Much more so than Russell Davies.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:46.550
Unless you count Kylie Minogue and Timothy
Dalton.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.540
Grant made Doctor Simeon feel like a real
threat to the Doctor without being too crazy

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:53.330
or over the top.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.200
I don’t know that we’ll ever get to see
him on the series again just because of what

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.240
they did with his character.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.050
As of the Series 7 finale he had become the
great intelligence, and I don’t know when

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.750
we’ll see that character again.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.780
Number 3 - Ian McKellen also in The Snowmen

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:11.510
I went a little bit nuts when I heard he was
playing a character, it made a little more

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:15.670
sense when I found out it was just providing
some voice over until Richard E Grant took

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:27.080
on the Great Intelligence Persona.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:33.650
But the way he made that giant snow globe
scary was so amazing.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:41.130
He’s gandalf after all, you shall not pass
without being blown away.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:46.020
Wouldn’t it be crazy if he did a brief walk
on cameo in a future special.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.550
It would lead to all kinds of Great Intelligence
paradox theories.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:52.360
Number 2 - Timothy Dalton in The End of Time

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:58.271
I think of all the big A list guest actors
and the characters they played he’s one

00:05:58.271 --> 00:05:59.860
of my favorite on both counts.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:04.930
There were some really cool guest actors like
David Morrisey who played really strange characters.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.370
Usually when they cast big people they give
them really big roles.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:11.060
But sometimes it just doesn’t work out the
way you want.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:15.370
It was like watching Shakespeare Doctor Who
in the best possible way.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:20.050
Dalton got to be the most infamous person
in the history of the canon next to The Omega

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:32.740
and The Master maybe and I feel like Russell
Davies just told him to go to town.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:39.690
When someone that good comes in usually directors
will give them notes on what they want or

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:43.370
help them stay on story, but what you get
from them is so amazing.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.280
They don’t need a lot of direction.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:50.130
You just sit and watch them melt your face
off with their monologues.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:53.880
His big cheer at the end of the first part
of End of Time is still one of my favorite

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:54.880
doctor who speeches ever.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.020
To the End of Time Itself.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:02.220
and my Number 1 favorite guest star on the
specials - Michael Gambon in A Christmas Carol

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:05.610
How awesome was it that Dumbledore agreed
to come on Doctor Who.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:11.150
I feel like for every big actor that we see,
10 turned the series down for whatever reason.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:14.830
But I feel like I don’t even need to say
too much about him as an actor.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.390
He’s one of the greatest living actors in
the world right now add to that, he also just

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:22.340
happens to live in the UK which makes it a
little easier to get to Cardiff to film Doctor

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:23.430
Who.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.800
There are a lot of amazing international actors
from everywhere but because of the way a lot

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:32.870
of British actors are brought up through the
theater, they have a distinct advantage in

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.590
genre shows like Doctor Who.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:40.840
Just as a personal preference I like Science
Fiction and Fantasy to be a little more theatrical.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:46.830
Even when it’s super depressing like Battlestar
it should still feel as up close and in your

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:48.590
face as a stage play.

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:53.500
That’s why some of the best moments from
Doctor Who so far have been Capaldi just talking

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:54.500
to himself.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.920
Because he can just carry a scene without
big explosions or special effects.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:01.500
And that requires a very special type of actor
that you don’t always find in America for

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.500
example.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:07.200
That’s one of the reasons I’m totally
fine with all the future doctor’s being

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.530
British, be the male or female.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:12.560
But now it’s your turn, let me know who
your favorite big guest actor has been in

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.560
all the specials.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.980
I suppose you could bend the rules and include
anyone from any kind of special, not just

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:21.590
the christmas episodes.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:25.250
The Q&amp;A will post tomorrow, if you want to
enter the giveaway all you have to do is be

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.400
a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:33.180
Generally giveaways are only for the team.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:39.919
So if you like to talk about Doctor Who, science
fiction or fantasy whatnot please join us.

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:43.979
Because I stayed up way too late last night
working on my Constantine video I was hallucinating

00:08:43.979 --> 00:08:45.560
a little during Time Heist today.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:48.410
To that effect here are a couple quick corrections
from my review.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.110
When I was talking about the architect, I
was thinking about the person who designed

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:56.670
the bank, not the architect of the plan to
rob said bank.

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:58.250
Which was the doctor.

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:00.660
And in regards to the next episode.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.000
Yes the doctor is the caretaker.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:08.170
Because American and British terms for schools
are different I was thinking Caretaker meant

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:12.300
Principal, which in the UK would be Headmaster.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.910
In America, the Caretaker of a school is called
the Janitor.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:18.243
I didn’t think the Doctor would be a janitor,
which is why I said headmaster.

00:09:18.243 --> 00:09:19.560
It’s just a wonky language thing.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.810
I’ll try to post the Q&amp;A early afternoon
pacific time.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.230
You can click here to get it.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:26.860
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it and you can check out my time heist review

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:27.860
right here.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.290
Thanks for watching, everybody high five quick
before I collapse from exhaustion.

